{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-seminormal-and-normalization}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d2a019b366f8f82f5a72e866023aac00b331adbde91648a0d4e4f200cefdfd3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLemma <REF_0001> motivates the\nfollowing definition. Since we have only constructed the\nnormalization in case <MATH_0001> locally has finitely many irreducible components,\nwe will also restrict ourselves to that case for the weak normalization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d7c021c408029633c1caa14c1d62b089b06f6c8554eb3d21323b827cdb53deb7", "unit_id": "tag:0H3I:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nX^\\nu \\longrightarrow X^{wn} \\longrightarrow X\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$X^\\nu$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$X^{wn} = X^{X^\\nu/wn}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-normalization}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-weak-normalization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b232e3ce283b160fa2c2c9e966d61acfeb1a0c989b3e5818cd7fc5102ce3ee7a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1edc7e4067c0d8e7655a484a94b4b1555b52007cd400ebeeec5301e7e520e742", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has\nfinitely many irreducible components. We define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>weak normalization<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> as the weak normalization\n<MATH_0003>\nof <MATH_0004> in the normalization <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>\n(Definition <REF_0001>).\nIn a formula: <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3039c790637e86430195433d5d1fba838d9fe0ee0873a20ed8eac7382579e8b", "unit_id": "tag:0H3R:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nX^\\nu \\to X^{wn} \\to X^{sn} \\to X\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-seminormal-and-normalization}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b964238a40f8cbbc8e38a456f0e435158dbf0b508dd0434ea9cc53c0dc37d25f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1d8b2e5e1d23b75b42f4ece027787376c89fe1befc10124666cc833401c15425", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nCombined with Lemma <REF_0001> we see that\nfor a scheme <MATH_0001> which locally has finitely many irreducible components\nthere are canonical morphisms\n<MATH_0002>\nHaving made this definition, we can say what it means for a scheme\nto be weakly normal (provided it has locally finitely many irreducible\ncomponents).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f2b2009a69139564469539efaf54916c8c61355786f6e50460bd53dde88f0b7", "unit_id": "tag:0H3I:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X^{wn} \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-weak-normalization}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-weakly-normal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:18835ad948cf57c18f755a21efaf165f88c28a7af52be9f10ecc20d8a7ea7fab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e63e8f13a2164e4132876cbd64eac64eb8f37fa3cea7cfcc57e5ce08815b709a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has\nfinitely many irreducible components. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>weakly normal<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif the weak normalization <MATH_0003> is an isomorphism\n(Definition <REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f4a6856c7d74163027983680c8371f16943c456ff3816a90cf6ee1d21678c212", "unit_id": "tag:0H3S:statement"}
